# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. bash treats a trailing CR as part of the
# command and fails with `$'\r': command not found`, so a Windows checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true, the default here) would rewrite scripts/release/*.sh to
# CRLF and they would stop running locally — while still working in CI, which
# is the worst version of this bug to debug.
*.sh text eol=lf
